    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d79-a1">

                <pb facs="0138" n="88" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg88"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 118.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McGarr to Mr.
                            Blanco.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-04-11"><hi rendition="#italic">April 11,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The commission for the settlement of claims
                    under the convention of August 7, 1892, between the United States and the
                    Republic of Chile, has expired by limitation after disposing of twenty-five
                    cases, and leaving eighteen claims undisposed of for want of time.</p>
                <pb facs="0139" n="89" xml:id="pg89"/>
                <p>My Government earnestly desires another commission to complete the work left
                    unfinished, and I am instructed to ascertain if your excellency’s Government,
                    animated by a like desire, will consent to a convention to create another
                    commission for the purpose indicated.</p>
                <p>Trusting to receive a favorable response, and with renewed assurances of my
                    highest consideration.</p>
                <p>I am etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Owen McGarr.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
